GET /notifications/threads/{thread_id}
Gets information about a notification thread.
Required: thread_id (path) — The unique identifier of the notification thread. This corresponds to the value returned in the `id` field when you retrieve notifications (for example with the [`GET /notifications` operation](https://docs.github.com/rest/activity/notifications#list-notifications-for-the-authenticated-user)).

DELETE /notifications/threads/{thread_id}
Marks a thread as "done." Marking a thread as "done" is equivalent to marking a notification in your notification inbox on GitHub as done: https://github.com/notifications.
Required: thread_id (path) — The unique identifier of the notification thread. This corresponds to the value returned in the `id` field when you retrieve notifications (for example with the [`GET /notifications` operation](https://docs.github.com/rest/activity/notifications#list-notifications-for-the-authenticated-user)).

PATCH /notifications/threads/{thread_id}
Marks a thread as "read." Marking a thread as "read" is equivalent to clicking a notification in your notification inbox on GitHub: https://github.com/notifications.
Required: thread_id (path) — The unique identifier of the notification thread. This corresponds to the value returned in the `id` field when you retrieve notifications (for example with the [`GET /notifications` operation](https://docs.github.com/rest/activity/notifications#list-notifications-for-the-authenticated-user)).
